###
### Church CMS API - Family Requests
### Use with IntelliJ IDEA HTTP Client or VS Code REST Client extension
###

### ===== CONFIGURATION =====
@keycloak_url = http://localhost:8080
@api_url = http://localhost:8081
@realm = church-cms
@client_id = church-cms-ui
@client_secret = 27074815-E8EF-469A-A183-DE11B802F90B
### The realm's default user has no ADMIN role; any authenticated user may create a family.
@username = john.doe
@password = 12345

### ===== AUTHENTICATION =====

### 1. Get Access Token from Keycloak
### The church is taken from the JWT organization_id claim; no specific role is required.
# @name getToken
POST {{keycloak_url}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password
&client_id={{client_id}}
&client_secret={{client_secret}}
&username={{username}}
&password={{password}}
&scope=email

> {% client.global.set("access_token", response.body.access_token); %}

### ===== CREATE FAMILIES =====

### 2. Create a family with only the required name (Should return 201)
### churchId, address, and weddingDate are omitted.
# @name createFamily
POST {{api_url}}/membership/families
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "name": "Doe"
}

> {% client.global.set("family_id", response.body.id); %}

### 3. Create a family with a complete address and wedding date (Should return 201)
POST {{api_url}}/membership/families
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "name": "Smith",
  "address": {
    "line1": "123 Main Street",
    "line2": "Suite 100",
    "city": "Springfield",
    "state": "Illinois",
    "country": "United States",
    "postalCode": "62701"
  },
  "weddingDate": "2005-06-18"
}

### 4. Request churchId is ignored (Should return 201 for the JWT's church)
### Change the churchId below to any other UUID; the response churchId stays the caller's.
POST {{api_url}}/membership/families
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "churchId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "name": "Johnson"
}

### 5. Name is trimmed (Should return 201 with "Brown")
POST {{api_url}}/membership/families
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "name": "   Brown   "
}

### ===== ERROR SCENARIOS =====

### 6. Name too short after trimming (Should return 400 with fieldErrors.name)
POST {{api_url}}/membership/families
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "name": "  Al  "
}

### 7. Name too long (Should return 400 with fieldErrors.name)
POST {{api_url}}/membership/families
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "name": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
}

### 8. Blank name (Should return 400 with fieldErrors.name)
POST {{api_url}}/membership/families
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "name": "   "
}

### 9. Missing address.line1 (Should return 400 with fieldErrors['address.line1'])
POST {{api_url}}/membership/families
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "name": "Doe Family",
  "address": {
    "city": "Springfield"
  }
}

### 10. Missing address.city (Should return 400 with fieldErrors['address.city'])
POST {{api_url}}/membership/families
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "name": "Doe Family",
  "address": {
    "line1": "123 Main Street"
  }
}

### 11. Too-short optional address field (Should return 400 with fieldErrors['address.line2'])
POST {{api_url}}/membership/families
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "name": "Doe Family",
  "address": {
    "line1": "123 Main Street",
    "line2": "ab",
    "city": "Springfield"
  }
}

### 12. Empty optional address fields are stored as null (Should return 201)
POST {{api_url}}/membership/families
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "name": "Williams",
  "address": {
    "line1": "456 Oak Avenue",
    "line2": "",
    "city": "Springfield",
    "state": "   ",
    "country": "",
    "postalCode": ""
  }
}

### 13. Malformed weddingDate (Should return 400)
POST {{api_url}}/membership/families
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "name": "Doe Family",
  "weddingDate": "18/06/2005"
}

### 14. Duplicate name in the same church (Should return 409 with conflictType=name)
### Request #2 created "Doe"; this case-variant must be rejected.
POST {{api_url}}/membership/families
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "name": "doe"
}

### 15. Unauthenticated request (Should return 401)
POST {{api_url}}/membership/families
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Doe"
}

### ===== NO READ ENDPOINT =====

### 16. Only POST /membership/families is exposed (GET returns no family data and is not 403)
GET {{api_url}}/membership/families/{{family_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### To verify the same name is allowed in another church, obtain a token with an
### organization_id claim for a different church and repeat request #2 with "Doe".
###
